   [1;36m│  §4 VERDICT — the hypothesis is REFUTED, and the truth is more useful    │[0m
   [1;36m╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯[0m
   [1mHypothesis:[0m "the solitons WERE the invisible mode; θ is Rhie–Chow-class
   stabilisation; its physical claim is NONE."

   [1;31mNo.[0m Every part of that is contradicted by a measurement with a control:

   1. [1mthere is no invisible mode to be.[0m water.rs is ALREADY STAGGERED — the head
      difference is taken across the face and the flux lives on the face. Its depth
      operator is the compact Laplacian; the checkerboard is its MOST-damped mode
      (§4A: 1 null mode, the constant; 0 spurious; ρ at Nyquist = 0.919 < 1).
      [1mThe Cardiff disease is the one disease this kernel does not have.[0m

   2. [1mthe solitons were a LONG WAVE, not a grid-scale mode.[0m The unstable mode of
      the pre-fix scheme sits at k/π = (0.33, 0.00) — a ~6-cell wave running ALONG
      the flow — while the Nyquist corner is quiet. That is the signature of a
      [1mROLL WAVE[0m, and roll waves are REAL PHYSICS above Fr ≈ 1.5 (Vedernikov).
      The base flow was at Fr 2.49. [1mThe scheme was RESOLVING an instability, not
      hallucinating one.[0m (What it got wrong is the SATURATION — a local-inertial
      scheme drops the advective term, so nothing bounds the wave.)

   3. [1mθ DOES NOT REMOVE THE MODE. It damps it, and it MOVES it.[0m
        θ = 1.0 → ρ = 1.04011   (48 growing modes, peak at k/π = 0.33)
        θ = 0.8 → ρ = 1.02655   (10 growing modes, peak at k/π = 0.17)  ← SHIPPED gain
        θ = 0.5 → ρ = 1.00775   ( 6 growing modes, peak at k/π = 0.17)
      Still unstable at HALF the shipped θ. And note where the peak goes: a low-pass
      filter cannot kill a long wave, so the instability simply [1mrelocates to the
      wavelengths the filter has no grip on.[0m θ buys time, not stability.

   4. [1mwhat actually stabilises the SHIPPED kernel is the JARRETT ROUGHNESS[0m — by
      dropping the flow from Fr 2.49 to Fr 0.75, i.e. out of the roll-wave regime
      entirely. Not θ. [1mThe credit was on the wrong term.[0m

   5. [1;33mAND THE JARRETT TERM HAS ITS OWN, PREVIOUSLY UNKNOWN INSTABILITY.[0m Because n
      rises with the local surface slope, a cell that gains water throttles its own
      outflow. On GENTLE slopes (where n has not yet saturated at the 0.13 cap) that
      loop is unstable at Fr ≈ 0.6 — nowhere near any roll-wave threshold. Hold n
      constant at the same magnitude and it vanishes (ρ 1.012 → 1.000). [1mThis one IS
      a numerical artefact with no physical claim[0m, and it is in the shipped kernel
      at exactly the slopes most of a landscape has.

   [1mNet for ASSUMPTIONS.md — the opposite of the proposed correction:[0m θ's physical
   claim is not NONE; it is damping a mode that is (partly) real, which means it may
   be suppressing PHYSICS. The term that deserves the hard look is the [1mJarrett
   proxy[0m, which MANUFACTURES an instability the physics does not have.

