[1m§5  THE PAYOFF — staggered vs collocated shallow water, same points, same grid[0m
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   The claim in doc/theory/fig/staggering.svg: a collocated scheme must reach TWO
   cells to get a flux across a face, so it computes (h_{i+1} − h_{i−1})/2Δ, which on
   the checkerboard is EXACTLY ZERO. A staggered scheme keeps the flux on the face
   it actually crosses and reaches only Δ. Same points. Same grid. Same cost.

   Tested on IDENTICAL linear shallow water (no friction — friction would hide the
   answer by damping everything): ∂f/∂t = −g·h̄·∇η ,  ∂d/∂t = −∇·f.

   Whole-operator null space (A = (J−I)/Δt):
   scheme                         zero σ   spectral gap
   ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   STAGGERED (flux on face)          146        1.1e299
   COLLOCATED (2Δ central)           152        1.0e299

   [1mBOTH numbers are large, and BOTH are mostly legitimate — so the raw count is[0m
   [1mnot the finding.[0m A wave system's null space contains every DIVERGENCE-FREE flux
   field (steady rotational flow: real, physical, and it should exert no force).
   The honest question is narrower and it is the one Cardiff is actually asking:

      [1mIs there a DEPTH field that exerts NO FORCE on the momentum equation?[0m

   That is the null space of the pressure-gradient block G = ∂(flux rate)/∂(depth),
   and a nonzero one is EXACTLY the checkerboard disease: a pressure/height pattern
   the scheme cannot feel, so nothing pushes back, so it grows without bound.

   scheme                      depth fields with     spurious   spectral gap
                                      ZERO force                            
   ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   STAGGERED (flux on face)                    1            0        1.1e300
   COLLOCATED (2Δ central)                     4 [1;31m           3[0m        1.0e300

   legitimate: 1 — the CONSTANT depth field (a uniform lift exerts no force; that
   is a rigid mode, exactly as Cardiff says it should be).

   ρ(J) staggered  = 1.000000   (a wave operator: |λ| = 1 for the WAVES — correct)
   ρ(J) collocated = 1.000000

